### Part 6: Failure Modes, Edge Cases & Complexity Matrix

```
+------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Failure Mode / Edge Case           | Architectural Mitigation Strategy                                                                  |
+------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| ABA Problem during Version Pruning | Tagged pointers combined with 3-Epoch quarantine. A node is never unlinked, recycled, or freed     |
|                                    | until all threads that could hold references have transitioned out of the retirement epoch.        |
+------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Reader Hang / Infinite Pinning     | Adaptive QSBR threshold (~15-20ms bound via `__rdtsc()`). If a thread exceeds the threshold, the   |
|                                    | engine switches to emergency Hazard Pointers (`hazard_ptr`), allowing global epoch advancement.   |
+------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| `io_uring` Short Writes & EAGAIN   | 4096-byte page alignment prevents unaligned DMA faults. Short writes are re-queued to the kernel   |
|                                    | ring via `file_offset + cqe->res` offset tracking before completing corresponding LSN promises.    |
+------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| CPU Cache Line Ping-Pong           | Critical per-thread state (`ThreadEpochState`) and MPSC ring pointers (`head_`, `tail_`) are       |
|                                    | padded with `alignas(64)` to eliminate false sharing.                                              |
+------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### Asymptotic Complexity Analysis

| Operation | Time Complexity (Best / Avg) | Time Complexity (Worst) | Synchronization Guarantee |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`search(key, read_ts)`** | $\mathcal{O}(\log N + V)$ | $\mathcal{O}(N + V)$ | **Wait-Free** (Deterministic bounded step count) |
| **`upsert(key, val)`** | $\mathcal{O}(\log N)$ | $\mathcal{O}(N)$ | **Lock-Free** (Global system progress invariant) |
| **`commit_version()`** | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ | $\mathcal{O}(V)$ | **Lock-Free** (Atomic compare-and-swap) |
| **`WAL Flush Pipeline`** | $\mathcal{O}(1)$ batched DMA | $\mathcal{O}(B)$ copy overhead | **Zero Syscall** (Kernel thread bypass via `SQPOLL`) |

*(Where $N$ is the number of distinct keys, $V$ is version chain depth, and $B$ is batch size in bytes).*

